SUMMARY:Revolutionary Art: A Conversation with the South Carolina State Ho
 use Tour Office
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261203T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261203T160000
UID:10003228-1796310000-1796313600@southcarolina250.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://southcarolina250.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2026/11/2026_10_22_09_16_11-scaled.jpg
CATEGORIES:Events
DESCRIPTION:Join the South Carolina State Library for a special event\, Re
 volutionary Art: A Conversation with the South Carolina State House Tour O
 ffice. Staff from the South Carolina State House Tour Office will discuss 
 the history and significance of the paintings in the South Carolina State 
 House\, including important battles and scenes from the American Revolutio
 n in South Carolina. They will also provide resources from various South C
 arolina State Parks and Historic Sites\, highlighting Revolutionary War hi
 story throughout the state.
LOCATION:South Carolina State Library\, 1500 Senate Street\, Columbia\, SC
 \, 29201\, United States
URL:https://southcarolina250.com/event/revolutionary-art-a-conversation-wi
 th-the-south-carolina-state-house-tour-office/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Revolutionary War Review Homeschool Friday - Battle of Eutaw Sprin
 gs
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261204T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261204T120000
UID:10003136-1796382000-1796385600@southcarolina250.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://southcarolina250.com/wp-content/uploads/2
 026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-01-153307.png
CATEGORIES:Lectures,Other
DESCRIPTION:December 4 – The Battle of Eutaw Springs\, SC (September 8\,
  1781). \nWe will be looking at the Battle of Eutaw Springs\, SC\, that wa
 s fought on September 8\, 1781. We’ll go over the various military units
  and leaders engaged in the fight as we examine the facts of the battle be
 fore\, during\, and after. Then\, we will track how this impacted the larg
 er course of the war. \nAs a part of our celebrations and remembrances dur
 ing the 250th\, the Anderson County Museum is adding a series to our Homes
 chool Friday program. \nThe Revolutionary War Review series will focus on 
 several elements of the Revolutionary War and is open to all students.
LOCATION:Anderson County Museum\, 202 East Greenville Street\, Anderson\, 
 SC\, 29621\, United States
URL:https://southcarolina250.com/event/revolutionary-war-review-homeschool
 -friday-battle-of-eutaw-springs/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:North Myrtle Beach Liberty Tree/Arbor Day Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261204T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261204T133000
UID:10003226-1796385600-1796391000@southcarolina250.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://southcarolina250.com/wp-content/uploads/2
 026/11/3DAC92D5-B92C-4107-8D48-1EC5859961CA.png
CATEGORIES:Anniversaries - Commemorations,Events
DESCRIPTION:December 4th 2026 at noon The City of North Myrtle Beach will 
 celebrate the 250 anniversary of the United States of America by unveiling
  a live oak that will henceforth be known as the City of North Myrtle Beac
 h’s Liberty Tree. \nThe Yaupon Garden Club and the NMB Tree Board are sp
 onsoring the event which will serve as the City’s Arbor Day Celebration.
  \nThis community event will be held at Mclean Park located in the heart o
 f North Myrtle Beach.
LOCATION:Mclean Park\, Main Street\, North Myrtle Beach SC\, SC\, 29582\, 
 United States
URL:https://southcarolina250.com/event/north-myrtle-beach-liberty-tree-arb
 or-day-celebration/
END:VEVENT
