BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Family Revolutionary Sunday: Surrender!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261213T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261213T150000
UID:10003190-1797170400-1797174000@southcarolina250.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://southcarolina250.com/wp-content/uploads/2
 026/09/Screenshot-2026-09-11-130712.png
CATEGORIES:Lectures,Other
DESCRIPTION:As 2026 draws to a close\, so do our Family Revolutionary Sund
 ays. Learn how the British were finally beaten and what the aftereffects o
 f Cornwallis’s surrender were in Charleston. In honor of the 250th anniv
 ersary of the signing of the Declaration of Independence\, The Charleston 
 Museum is hosting a series of family programs called Revolutionary Sundays
  throughout 2026. These free with admission or Museum membership programs 
 will explore different themes\, events\, and people from the Revolutionary
  War. Revolutionary Sundays include a class or guided tour and a craft or 
 activity. \nFREE for Members and FREE with admission to The Charleston Mus
 eum \nFor more information: call 843-722-2996 ext. 236
LOCATION:The Charleston Museum\, 360 Meeting Street\, Charleston\, SC\, 29
 403\, United States
URL:https://southcarolina250.com/event/family-revolutionary-sunday-surrend
 er/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Behind Enemy Lyrics
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261215T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261215T130000
UID:10003229-1797336000-1797339600@southcarolina250.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://southcarolina250.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2026/11/Behind-Enemy-Lyrics_CALENDAR.jpg
CATEGORIES:Lectures
DESCRIPTION:Join Rev. John Paul Marr at the Anderson County Museum as we e
 xplore the revolutionary warfare of words. 18th century broadsheet lyrics 
 functioned as part of the ideological propaganda machine for both the Brit
 ish and the Patriots. The stories of these songs and their rippling effect
 s provide another perspective for understanding the founding of the United
  States of America. Hear the tunes and experience the back-and-forth battl
 es of singing the songs of the American Revolution.
LOCATION:Anderson County Museum\, 202 East Greenville Street\, Anderson\, 
 SC\, 29621\, United States
URL:https://southcarolina250.com/event/behind-enemy-lyrics/
END:VEVENT
