BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eliza - An American Opera
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261216T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261216T213000
UID:10003224-1797449400-1797456600@southcarolina250.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://southcarolina250.com/wp-content/uploads/2
 026/10/90053638-F978-40F2-A857-97A3B8A0318C.png
CATEGORIES:Events,Other
DESCRIPTION:ELIZA: A Chamber Opera brings to life the courage\, enterprise
 \, and resilience of free\, enslaved\, and freed African and African-desce
 nded market women in relationship with Jewish Femme Soles in Revolutionary
 -era Charleston\, South Carolina. \nCommissioned by the Jonathan Green Mar
 itime Cultural Center at the University of South Carolina Beaufort and spo
 nsored in part by the SC250 Commission\, the opera explores women’s role
 s in commerce\, community\, and the pursuit of freedom.
LOCATION:Koger Center for the Performing Arts at the University of South C
 arolina Columbia\, 1051 Greene St.\, Columbia\, SC\, 29201\, United States
URL:https://southcarolina250.com/event/eliza-an-american-opera/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Revolutionary War Review Homeschool Friday - The Surrender at York
 town
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261218T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261218T120000
UID:10003135-1797591600-1797595200@southcarolina250.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://southcarolina250.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2026/08/Surrender_of_Lord_Cornwallis.jpg
CATEGORIES:Lectures,Other
DESCRIPTION:December 18 – The Battle and Surrender at Yorktown (October 
 19\, 1781). \nWe will be looking at the battle\, siege\, and surrender at 
 Yorktown. After a siege\, the British forces surrendered on October 19\, 1
 781. Come learn why. We’ll go over the various military units and leader
 s engaged in the fight as we examine the facts of the battle before\, duri
 ng\, and after. Then\, we will track how this impacted the larger course o
 f the war. \nAs a part of our celebrations and remembrances during the 250
 th\, the Anderson County Museum is adding a series to our Homeschool Frida
 y program. \nThe Revolutionary War Review series will focus on several ele
 ments of the Revolutionary War and is open to all students.
LOCATION:Anderson County Museum\, 202 East Greenville Street\, Anderson\, 
 SC\, 29621\, United States
URL:https://southcarolina250.com/event/revolutionary-war-review-homeschool
 -friday-the-surrender-at-yorktown/
END:VEVENT
