SUMMARY:THE BATTLE OF CAMDEN (Theatre)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270122T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270131T193000
UID:10003202-1800646200-1801423800@southcarolina250.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://southcarolina250.com/wp-content/uploads/2
 026/09/BattleofCamden.png
CATEGORIES:Performance
DESCRIPTION:THE BATTLE OF CAMDEN\nPlay by Tony Scully\nDirected by Tracy S
 teele \nJanuary 22-31\, 2027\nFREE TO THE PUBLIC\nLocation: Black Box Thea
 tre\nSPONSORED BY SC250 & DUKE ENERGY FOUNDATION\n& LINDA & JOHN SHAYLOR \
 nTHE ROAD TO AMERICAN INDEPENDENCE RAN THROUGH CAMDEN \nExperience a power
 ful retelling of one of the Revolutionary War’s most pivotal moments wit
 h The Battle of Camden. This moving production brings history to life thro
 ugh the voices of those who shaped — and survived — the Battle of Camd
 en. \nThis show is free to the public\, but reservations are required due 
 to limited seating. https://artscenterkc.org/ac/the-battle-of-camden/ \nTh
 e Arts Center Revolutionary Series is made possible through grant support 
 from the South Carolina American Revolution Sestercentennial Commission an
 d the Duke Energy Foundation.
LOCATION:Arts Center of Kershaw County\, 810 Lyttleton St.\, Camden\, SC\,
  29020\, United States
URL:https://southcarolina250.com/event/the-battle-of-camden-theatre/
END:VEVENT
